  "body": "If on google.com and trying to set a cookie with the domain \"GoOGLe.com\":\n\n`document.cookie=\"CookieName=CookieValue; domain=GoOGLe.com; path=/\";`\nwill create a cookie with the domain \"google.com\". \n\nBut:\n\n`cookieStore.set({ name: \"CookieName\", value: \"cookieValue\", domain: \"GoOGLe.com\", path: \"/\" })`\nresults in an error that says the passed in domain doesn't match the context's domain. The spec doesn't say to modify the domain before comparing it to the context's domain.\n\nShould the Cookie Store puny code the domain (or convert it to lowercase) before checking it against the context's domain?",
